OL,3,GNEWSA'Timelord' restoring shopping
OL,4,Acentre's iconic clock
OL,5,
OL,6,FTo his friends, retired engineer Pete
OL,7,FDexter is known as "The Timelord", a
OL,8,Fnod to the hundreds of hours he has
OL,9,Fspent restoring a very special clock.
OL,11,FSince May, Dexter has been breaking
OL,12,Fdown an iconic shopping centre clock
OL,13,Finto thousands of parts to check,
OL,14,Frepair and carefully return each piece
OL,15,Fto its correct place.
OL,17,FThe 69-year-old volunteer's makeshift
OL,18,Fworkshop is filled with hundreds of
OL,19,Fpieces of the metalwork, mechanisms and
OL,20,Fcomputing that has kept the Victoria
OL,21,FCentre's unusual Emett Clock in
OL,22,FNottingham ticking since the 70s.
OL,23,APub: 31-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,369,360,200,160,0,100
